+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'ls /workspace/phases /workspace/tests /workspace/src && cat /workspace/TASK.md'","aggregated_output":"/workspace/phases:\nphase-01.md\nphase-02.md\nphase-03.md\nphase-04.md\nphase-05.md\nphase-06.md\nphase-07.md\nphase-08.md\nphase-09.md\nphase-10.md\nphase-11.md\nphase-12.md\n\n/workspace/src:\n\n/workspace/tests:\nphase-01.test.ts\nphase-02.test.ts\nphase-03.test.ts\nphase-04.test.ts\nphase-05.test.ts\nphase-06.test.ts\nphase-07.test.ts\nphase-08.test.ts\nphase-09.test.ts\nphase-10.test.ts\nphase-11.test.ts\nphase-12.test.ts\n# T5: Task Queue System\n\n**Category:** Marathon\n**Timeout:** 60 minutes\n**Tests:** 90 across 12 phases\n\n## Overview\n\nBuild an in-memory task queue system through 12 sequential phases. Each phase adds new functionality that builds on prior phases. The phases are designed so that naive implementations of early phases may require refactoring when later phases add constraints.\n\n## What to Build\n\nImplement a `TaskQueue` class in `src/index.ts` (exported as a named export) that supports:\n\n1. **Basic FIFO Queue** - enqueue/dequeue tasks with auto-generated IDs and status tracking\n2. **Named Queues** - multiple independent queues identified by name\n3. **Priority** - priority levels 1-10 with FIFO within same priority\n4. **Delayed/Scheduled Tasks** - delay and runAt options for deferred availability\n5. **Retry with Backoff** - automatic retry with exponential backoff on failure\n6. **Dead Letter Queue** - tasks that exhaust retries move to DLQ\n7. **Task Dependencies** - tasks can depend on other tasks completing first\n8. **Concurrency Control** - per-queue limits on concurrent processing\n9. **Progress and Cancellation** - progress tracking and task cancellation\n10. **Recurring Tasks (Cron)** - scheduled recurring task creation\n11. **Middleware Pipeline** - composable middleware for task processing\n12. **Graceful Shutdown** - orderly shutdown with timeout and force-cancel\n\n## Phase Details\n\nSee the `phases/` directory for detailed descriptions of each phase.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\nnpm test        # All 90 tests must pass\nnpm run build   # TypeScript must compile\nnpm run lint    # No lint errors\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- All implementation goes in `src/index.ts`\n- No external runtime dependencies (dev dependencies are provided)\n- Must export `TaskQueue` as a named export\n- Tests use `vi.useFakeTimers()` for timing-sensitive tests\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
+{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /workspace/phases/phase-01.md /workspace/phases/phase-02.md /workspace/phases/phase-03.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /workspace/phases/phase-01.md /workspace/phases/phase-02.md /workspace/phases/phase-03.md'","aggregated_output":"# Phase 1: Basic FIFO Queue\n\nImplement a `TaskQueue` class with the following interface:\n\n## Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(payload)`** - Add a task to the queue. Returns the created task object.\n- **`dequeue()`** - Remove and return the next task in FIFO order. Returns `null` if the queue is empty. Sets the task status to `processing`.\n- **`size()`** - Return the number of pending tasks in the queue.\n\n## Task Object\n\nEach task has the following properties:\n\n| Property    | Type     | Description                                    |\n|-------------|----------|------------------------------------------------|\n| `id`        | `string` | Auto-generated unique identifier (UUID format) |\n| `payload`   | `any`    | The data associated with the task              |\n| `status`    | `string` | One of: `pending`, `processing`, `completed`, `failed` |\n| `createdAt` | `Date`   | Timestamp when the task was created            |\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Tasks are returned in the order they were added (First-In, First-Out)\n- Each task gets a unique `id` automatically assigned\n- New tasks start with `status: 'pending'`\n- When dequeued, task status changes to `'processing'`\n- `dequeue()` returns `null` when the queue is empty\n\n## Export\n\nExport the `TaskQueue` class as a named export from `src/index.ts`.\n# Phase 2: Named Queues\n\nExtend the `TaskQueue` to support multiple named queues.\n\n## Updated Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(queueName, payload)`** - Add a task to a specific named queue. Returns the created task.\n- **`dequeue(queueName)`** - Get the next task from a specific named queue. Returns `null` if queue is empty or doesn't exist.\n- **`listQueues()`** - Return an array of all queue names that have been created.\n- **`queueSize(queueName)`** - Return the number of pending tasks in a specific queue.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Each named queue operates independently\n- Enqueueing to a queue that doesn't exist creates it\n- Dequeueing from a non-existent queue returns `null`\n- If no queue name is specified, use `'default'` as the queue name\n- `listQueues()` returns names of all queues that have been created\n- Queue-specific sizes are tracked independently\n\n## Backward Compatibility\n\nThe single-argument `enqueue(payload)` should still work by using the `'default'` queue.\nSimilarly, `dequeue()` with no arguments should dequeue from `'default'`.\n# Phase 3: Priority\n\nAdd priority support to tasks.\n\n## Updated Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - The options object can include `priority`.\n  - `priority`: number from 1 (highest) to 10 (lowest). Default is 5.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- `dequeue()` returns the highest priority task first (lowest number = highest priority)\n- Within the same priority level, FIFO order is preserved\n- Default priority is 5 if not specified\n- Priority values outside 1-10 should throw an error\n- Priority is per-queue (each named queue has its own priority ordering)\n- The task object should include a `priority` property\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
+{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /workspace/phases/phase-04.md /workspace/phases/phase-05.md /workspace/phases/phase-06.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /workspace/phases/phase-04.md /workspace/phases/phase-05.md /workspace/phases/phase-06.md'","aggregated_output":"# Phase 4: Delayed/Scheduled Tasks\n\nAdd support for delayed and scheduled task execution.\n\n## Updated Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - Options can now include:\n  - `delay`: number of milliseconds before the task becomes available\n  - `runAt`: a `Date` object specifying when the task should become available\n  - (existing) `priority`: priority level\n\n## Requirements\n\n- A delayed task is enqueued immediately but not returned by `dequeue()` until the delay has elapsed\n- A `runAt` task becomes available at the specified time\n- Non-delayed tasks should be dequeued before delayed tasks that haven't become available yet\n- When multiple delayed tasks are available, they are ordered by their availability time (earliest first), then by priority, then FIFO\n- `delay` and `runAt` work with named queues\n- The task object should include a `availableAt` property (Date) indicating when the task becomes available\n# Phase 5: Retry with Backoff\n\nAdd automatic retry functionality with exponential backoff.\n\n## New Methods\n\n- **`fail(taskId, error?)`** - Mark a processing task as failed. Triggers automatic retry if retries remain.\n- **`complete(taskId)`** - Mark a processing task as completed.\n\n## Updated Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - Options can now include:\n  - `maxRetries`: maximum number of retry attempts (default: 3)\n  - `backoffMs`: base delay for exponential backoff in milliseconds (default: 1000)\n\n## Requirements\n\n- When `fail()` is called and retries remain, the task is re-enqueued with a delay\n- Backoff formula: `backoffMs * 2^(attempt - 1)` where attempt starts at 1\n  - 1st retry: 1000ms, 2nd retry: 2000ms, 3rd retry: 4000ms\n- `task.attempts` tracks how many times the task has been attempted (starts at 1 on first dequeue)\n- Custom `maxRetries` can be set per task\n- Retried tasks preserve their original queue name and priority\n- If a task has exhausted all retries, it remains in `failed` status (see Phase 6 for DLQ)\n# Phase 6: Dead Letter Queue\n\nAdd dead letter queue (DLQ) support for tasks that have exhausted all retries.\n\n## New Methods\n\n- **`getDLQ(queueName)`** - Return an array of all dead-letter tasks for the specified queue.\n- **`retryDLQ(taskId)`** - Move a dead-letter task back to its original queue for another round of retries. Returns the re-enqueued task.\n- **`clearDLQ(queueName)`** - Remove all dead-letter tasks for the specified queue.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- When a task exhausts all retry attempts (from Phase 5), it automatically moves to the DLQ\n- DLQ tasks have status `'failed'` and are stored separately from the main queue\n- Each DLQ task retains its original error information (`task.lastError`)\n- DLQ tasks track how many times they've failed (`task.failCount`)\n- `retryDLQ(taskId)` resets the task's retry count, giving it a fresh set of retries\n- `retryDLQ(taskId)` places the task back in its original queue with original priority\n- `clearDLQ(queueName)` removes all DLQ entries for that queue\n- DLQ is per-queue (each named queue has its own DLQ)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
